-- title:
--   Finiteness of Pic⁰[n] and finite level of its Galois action
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure which is essentially of finite type over $\mathbb{Q}$ and satisfies `IsCurveOver ℚ F`, i.e. every nonzero element of $F$ has an associated divisor of degree $0$ recording its orders at all places, every place of $F$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ has residue field finite over $\mathbb{Q}$, and $\Omega_{F/\mathbb{Q}}$ is free of rank one over $F$; let $\bar F$ be a field with the analogous data over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`. Let $\mathrm{toBar} : F \to \bar F$ be a ring homomorphism compatible with $\mathbb{Q} \to F$ and $\mathbb{Q} \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}} \to \bar F$, such that the subfield of $\bar F$ generated by the images of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ and of $\mathrm{toBar}$ is all of $\bar F$, and such that every finite subset of $F$ that is $\mathbb{Q}$-linearly independent has $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-linearly independent image. Let $\mathrm{gal}$ be a group homomorphism from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\bar{\mathbb{Q}})$ to the group of pairs $(\tau, \tau_0) \in \mathrm{Aut}(\bar F) \times \mathrm{Aut}(\bar{\mathbb{Q}})$ with $\tau(a \cdot 1) = \tau_0(a)\cdot 1$, whose second component at $\sigma$ is $\sigma$ itself and which fixes $\mathrm{toBar}(x)$ for every $x \in F$. Then, firstly, for every $n > 0$ the $n$-torsion subgroup of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(\bar F/\bar{\mathbb{Q}})$ (degree-zero divisors modulo principal ones) is finite; secondly, for every $n > 0$ there is an intermediate field $L$ of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$, finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$, such that every $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise acts trivially, through $\mathrm{gal}$, on every $n$-torsion class.
--
--   This supplies the two arithmetic finiteness properties of the Jacobian-like object $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of a curve over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ obtained by base change from $\mathbb{Q}$: finiteness of $n$-torsion and the fact that the Galois action on it factors through a finite extension. It is used in the construction of Shimura curve models in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where these two properties are required of every model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_finite_pic0Torsion_and_exists_intermediateField_smul_eq_of_descent.lean

